## Bug Description
During streamed response delivery (live token streaming) on Telegram, if the streamed message content grows past Telegram's 4096-character limit, the gateway enters an infinite nested reply loop, sending the same content over and over as nested reply messages.

## Root Cause
In `gateway/platforms/telegram.py`, the pre-flight check for message length:
```python
if utf16_len(content) > self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH:
    return await self._edit_overflow_split(
        chat_id, message_id, content, finalize=finalize, metadata=metadata,
    )
```
runs *unconditionally* for every streamed edit (even when `finalize=False`). 

Since `_edit_overflow_split` edits Chunk 1 and sends Chunk 2 as a new reply (and updates the active message ID to the new continuation ID), on the very next token chunk receipt the stream consumer tries to edit the new active message with the *entire* accumulated text. Because the text still exceeds 4096 characters, it splits *again*, leading to a chain of duplicate replies for every single streamed token from the model after the limit is hit.

## Fix
Make the pre-flight split check conditional on `finalize`. Mid-stream, if the content exceeds the maximum length, edit the message with truncated content (cut at 4000 code units) to keep the preview updating without spawning continuation messages until the stream completes (`finalize=True`). On `finalize=True`, do the actual `_edit_overflow_split` call to cleanly send all segments.

Proposed changes applied locally:
```python
        if utf16_len(content) > self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH:
            if finalize:
                return await self._edit_overflow_split(
                    chat_id, message_id, content, finalize=finalize, metadata=metadata,
                )
            else:
                # Mid-stream: temporarily truncate content to avoid spamming splits
                # and continue editing the first chunk until finalize is called.
                truncated = self.truncate_message(content, self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH, len_fn=utf16_len)[0]
                try:
                    await self._bot.edit_message_text(
                        chat_id=int(chat_id),
                        message_id=int(message_id),
                        text=truncated,
                    )
                except Exception as stream_err:
                    if "not modified" not in str(stream_err).lower():
                        logger.warning(
                            "[%s] Mid-stream overflow edit failed: %s",
                            self.name, stream_err,
                        )
                return SendResult(success=True, message_id=message_id)
```
This resolves the replication loops entirely.
